            <ArticleTitle>Osseous fragment in a patient with knee pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>323</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.2519/jospt.2015.0404</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The patient was a 31-year-old man who was currently serving in the military. He was referred to a physical therapist by his primary care physician for a chief complaint of left anterior knee pain. Due to concern over a loose body, the physical therapist ordered radiographs of the left knee, which revealed an osseous fragment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
